@@ -45,6 +45,21 @@ by actual upstream interface.
 
 ## Resolver Handoff
 
+Before resolver selection, one ordinary IN question for the exact name
+`vpnhotspot.lan` (case insensitive) is answered locally. A queries receive the
+actual downstream IPv4 gateway selected by the existing netlink address query,
+with a five-second TTL. Other types receive NODATA. Gateway absence, ambiguity,
+or a five-second address lookup timeout yields SERVFAIL; unexpected netlink
+errors are reported as `dns.dashboard_gateway`. Unrelated names retain the
+existing upstream/fallback resolver path. Local replies do not increase upstream
+DNS counters and work without an available upstream.
+
+This adds no listener, address, route, firewall rule, or persistent root state.
+The per-query netlink connection is dropped after lookup; normal stop/Clean and
+process death keep the existing DNS listener cleanup behavior. HTTP stays in
+the unprivileged app process. Clients bypassing this DNS handler must use the
+numeric downstream gateway URL.
+
 DNS queries are sent through bionic's Android resolver API:
 
 - `android_res_nsend` starts a one-shot query on the selected Android network;
